# Implemented

Added payload-free, cached read-only projection of private runtime-input queue
health. It reports known queued count, oldest original queue age, incomplete
ownership-history line and partial coverage. It explicitly reports that launcher
hold is unobserved; no queue, cursor, lifecycle status, event-ack/1 receipt, or
injection is changed.

# Surfaces

- `GET /ca/chat/delivery-health` and additive `delivery` in request responses.
- Receiver public status includes `status.delivery`.
- TUI status includes `delivery`; the TUI page distinguishes observation SSE
  connectivity from session delivery state.
- External-event menu and generated statusline show informational delivery state.

# Evidence

Focused exact-file tests passed on 2026-10-21 in clean temporary state:
`test_runtime_input_delivery_health.py` (8), `test_chat_http_injection_mode.py`
(16), `test_external_event_receiver.py` (13), `test_statusline.py` (15), and
`test_event_delivery_ack.py` (33). Python compilation passed for all changed
modules. Existing TUI integration test
`test_routed_sse_turn_is_available_from_recent_api` timed out twice at its
2-second HTTP response deadline, including with isolated CIEL_RUNTIME paths.
Cause not established; it was not treated as a delivery-health pass.


# Integration boundary

TUI HTTP ports accept an additive optional `delivery_health` callback. The facade
owner must wire it to the status repository and actual private input path. Chat
request APIs infer that repository from their existing bound `request_status`
method; receivers infer it from the bound gateway `submit_external_event`.
No facade edits are included in this work unit.

# Runtime evidence

The focused suite starts an actual ThreadingHTTPServer on an ephemeral loopback
port, requests `/ca/channel/requests/1`, observes `ok=true`, lifecycle `queued`,
and additive `delivery.state=admission_blocked`, then verifies source file bytes
are unchanged. A generated statusline subprocess runs outside the package cwd
and renders `session delivery admission_blocked` with the physical failure line.
A connected receiver remains `state=connected` while its separate delivery
observation is blocked. No live session or external endpoint was altered.
